source: /mnt/mtwo/programming/ai-stuff/delta-version/scripts/libs/llama-chat-client.lua
commit: f12d85693838a3ddf3b0e6bcfce89fe018e96f42
copied: 2026-11-05
changes: this project's own, made in the copy (issue 401b):
         - dkjson is found beside this file (libs/dkjson.lua), not through
           AISTUFF_ROOT, so nothing outside the project is loaded.
         - every call takes an endpoint record { name, url, timeout }
           instead of one configured host and port; configure() and the
           INFERENCE_CHAT_HOST override are gone, so each role reaches its
           own endpoint and nothing can re-point it from the environment.
         - an embedding call, embed(endpoint, texts), on /v1/embeddings.
         - chat() also returns the whole decoded reply (for the token usage).
         - the unreachable message points at scripts/start-servers.
         - the CLI takes --url URL and --timeout SECONDS.
         - an endpoint's key, when it has one, goes as an Authorization
           bearer header, from a temporary file curl reads (-H @file), so
           it is never on a command line (issue 402).
